This is NOT an open-source licence. The sources are published for reading, not
for use.

COVERED: all project code, shaders, artwork in `art/`, the text of `README.md`
and other design notes, the game itself and its name.

YOU MAY, without asking:
  — read the sources, study how it works, and learn from them;
  — play the demo and show it to others;
  — fork the repository through GitHub (GitHub's own terms allow this, and it
    cannot be forbidden while the repository stays public).

YOU MAY NOT, without the author's written permission:
  — use the code, shaders or artwork in your own projects, in whole or in part;
  — distribute the game or builds of it, modified or not;
  — use anything here commercially;
  — train models on these files.

If you want any of the above, contact the author through GitHub.

THIRD PARTY. The game is built with the Godot Engine, which is distributed
under the MIT licence and belongs to its own authors. This copyright does not
extend to the engine: built games contain its code, and distributing them
requires keeping the Godot copyright notice (the engine shows it itself, in its
licence screen). Export templates are not part of this repository.

CO-AUTHORSHIP. Part of the project history contains commits by another person
(Mikhail Koshkin). Rights to their contribution belong to them; this notice
neither cancels nor transfers those rights.
